From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: lpass-tx-macro: route TX SMIC MUX0 SWR_MIC10/11 to their own inputs

TX SMIC MUX0 routes SWR_MIC10 to "TX SWR_INPUT11" and SWR_MIC11 to
"TX SWR_INPUT10"; MUX1..MUX7 map each SWR_MICn to "TX SWR_INPUTn". The
mux register selects SoundWire line 10 for SWR_MIC10, so DAPM powered the
codec path behind the other input: with the codec mic routed to
"TX SWR_INPUT10", DEC0 on SWR_MIC10 either never powered (no data, -EIO
from the DSP) or powered a path that was not the one being read. Map
MUX0 the same way as the other muxes.

Tested on the Retroid Pocket Nova (WCD938x DMIC6 on SWR_MIC10).

Fixes: d34f0c8ee2e3 ("ASoC: codecs: tx-macro: correct TX SMIC MUXn widgets on SM8350+")
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
@@ -1916,8 +1916,8 @@
 	{"TX SMIC MUX0", "SWR_MIC7", "TX SWR_INPUT7"},
 	{"TX SMIC MUX0", "SWR_MIC8", "TX SWR_INPUT8"},
 	{"TX SMIC MUX0", "SWR_MIC9", "TX SWR_INPUT9"},
-	{"TX SMIC MUX0", "SWR_MIC10", "TX SWR_INPUT11"},
-	{"TX SMIC MUX0", "SWR_MIC11", "TX SWR_INPUT10"},
+	{"TX SMIC MUX0", "SWR_MIC10", "TX SWR_INPUT10"},
+	{"TX SMIC MUX0", "SWR_MIC11", "TX SWR_INPUT11"},
 
 	{"TX DEC1 MUX", "SWR_MIC", "TX SMIC MUX1"},
 	{"TX SMIC MUX1", NULL, "TX_SWR_CLK"},
